  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "S2 keeps a 7% permanent limit (above the 5% benchmark), which admits Northwind's Hearth 10 at 6.2%, and keeps per-model results out of public publication while giving them to purchasers and regulators. S5 sets a mandatory recall at 8 per 100,000 with no transition, which would hit Halcyon's Ember 8 at 9.9, though the open-ended corrective-action alternative is ambiguous. S1 imposes a 24-hour reporting duty that covers unreported incidents at both companies, and S4 sets built-in suppression at 36 months."
